Z||000007||Monkeyman||11-16-2001||08:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by avengador1:<BR><B>I've seen it before. It has a Suzuki motorcycle engine. As for reverse it has an electric starter motor to drive it backwards.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope.  Volkswagen all the way.  Little brother to the totally awesome Patriot.  (The entire roof/hood/sides open up clam shell style.)  This is one of the easiest kits to build.  Basically, there are only two parts.  The inner tub (interior) and the body.  You remove the VW body (any Standard Beetle will work, but not the Super due to the McPherson strut front suspension) and interior, bolt the inner tub on, bolt the misc parts to the interior (gauges, seats, switches, etc), bolt the outer shell on, wheels, tires, etc and you're set.<P>This kit and it's big brother are built/marketed by a small company with 3 letters (like DMC for Delorean).  I just can't remember the name of the company.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroX||11-17-2001||05:12 AM||||the car is marketed and sold by thunder ranch.  655 Front Street, El Cajon CA, 92020.  (619)444-1006.  Retails for $3,650.  <BR>(I just so happened to have an old issue of Kit car sitting right next to me when I saw this thread)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
