Z||000010||avengador1||11-17-2001||01:25 PM||||The picture above is the second generation of this kit. The original had a Suzuki 1100 engine as I stated, and was a smaller car.It also used a lot of the motorcycles parts. I think it even looked better than this one, because this one was streched to fit a VW pan. The first riot was yellow and was built on a tubular chassis. I guess he (Tom Mc Burnie) re-engineered the kit to make it easier to build, and get rid of problems the original had (starter motor that engaged a sprocket for reverse). There is a write up of the VW based kit, made by Thunder Ranch in El Cajon CA, in the September 1996 issue of KIT CAR magazine, on page number 84. I will try to find the article on the original kit and post some pictures or specs if I find it. ||||reg||1
